  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "For real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y,\\) define \\[x \\spadesuit y = (x + y)(x - y).\\] What is \\(3 \\spadesuit (4 \\spadesuit 5)?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-72\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-27\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(-24\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(24\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(72\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "-72"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2006-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(x \\spadesuit y = x^2 - y^2,\\) the inner value is \\(4 \\spadesuit 5 = 16 - 25 = -9.\\)\n\nThen \\(3 \\spadesuit (-9) = 3^2 - (-9)^2\\) \\(= 9 - 81 = -72.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Note that \\(x \\spadesuit y = x^2 - y^2\\)",
        "Evaluate the inner \\(4 \\spadesuit 5\\) first, then apply the operation again"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
